==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Sathankhamun VIII]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Nimoy Bore]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 8~10 seconds<sup>240f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Chickful A]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*10 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 6~8 seconds<sup>180f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*15 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 6~8 seconds<sup>180f~240f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Nimoy Bore]]s spawn after 366.67 seconds<sup>11,000f</sup>, delay 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mr. Puffington]]s spawn after 450 seconds<sup>13,500f</sup>, delay 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**2 [[Chickful A]]s spawn, delay 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.
**5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main strategy used for this stage is to kill Nimoy Bore, Puffington and Chickful A quickly, while using this opportunity to damage the boss. Once these enemies are gone, [[Sathankhamun VIII]] is no longer a threat and can be taken down safely.

Due to how cash-tight and aggressive this stage can get, it is recommended to use a Rich Cat, Sniper the Cat and the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast Cannon|Breakerblast Cannon]].

The [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]] adds extra difficulty here, so beating [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku Invasion]] is recommended.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] - Produces [[Wave Attack]]s frequently when used well on Cerberus Kids, allowing it to consistently deal heavy damage to Chickful A, Sathankamun, Nimoy Bore and Puffington. However, the damage can unintentionally reset Puffington's attack animation.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]]/[[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill]]/[[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]]/[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]] - Used to fight Nimoy Bore at the beginning and quickly kill him so you can secure as much ground as possible.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Somewhat of a last resort option, Bahamut is difficult to use, but can be rewarding if he manages to hit Chickful A or Puffington at least once, taking almost a quarter of their health. If his Explosion Talent is maxed, he can secure even more damage on them.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Well-timed Bullet Trains should be used to specifically damage Chickful A so you have an easier time with Puffington.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - Manic Eraser is obviously useful, but once the pressure grows Boulder (due to having extreme health and Slow Immunity) will be needed to stop enemies from gaining too much ground.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - Used to slow the boss and other enemies occasionally, giving you a little more breathing room.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] - One of the best responses to Puffington, the most annoying enemy in this stage; a level 40 Idi deals enough damage to kill him in two hits. If timed well such that Puffington is ahead and she gets to land a second hit, the rest of the stage is much easier.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] - Doron is able to disable Puffington for several seconds. The [[Surge Attack]] does enough damage to actually knock him back, kill Cerberus Kids and chip other enemies, while also exposing Chickful A and puts her in the line of fire for your attackers to hit.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]/[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]] - As you probably expect, a stage where Awakened Bahamut does well is also a stage where they does well. Though Oni Battlepod is great against Chickful A but is vulnerable to Curse.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]] - His Slow Immunity and Resistant Vs Aku let him walk to Sathankhamun (if you cleared path for him) and deliver Massive Damage attacks that can two-shot boss at level 46+. Keep in mind he is still vulnerable to Curse.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] - Gravolodon is a perfect unit for this level. With its strong Wave Attacks, cheap cost, fast recharge, [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] abilities, high base hp, and even a Defense [[Cat Combo|Combo]] with [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]], Gravolodon can function as a defensive Jellycat that can take care of Nimoy Bore, can deal great chip damage, and can survive for a good amount of time. With Talents, Gravolodon can also gain a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] target and immunity to Knockback.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] - While there are no [[Shield]]s in the level, Kai still does great at staying on the field for a while and dealing loads of damage to the boss. If you happen to have her Target Aku and [[Curse Immunity]] [[Ultra Talents]], she becomes an even more durable wall. She also has a defense Combo with [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], which helps with the battle overall.
*[[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]] - Another great unit for this level, he is a useful tanker and a weak Wave Attacker for every enemy except for Puffington. Just make sure you send him out after the first Puffington, as Puffington's curse renders him useless.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]] - Essentially a second Breakerblast Cannon, Lunos's target traits and [[Conjure]] allow him to beat down threats or regain ground as needed. Thanks to his [[Resistant|Resistance]] and [[Immune to Slow]], Lunos can freely walk up to Sathankhamun and many of the supporting enemies. However, Lunos does not target [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], so it may be best not to use him until Nimoy Bore is down. At Lv.50, after you deal with the initial Nimoy Bore, he can solo the rest of the stage.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] - Thanks to their absurd anti-Traited damage, Dawnbringer Izanagi can nuke all the major threats in the stage for an easy win, using the supporting enemies as stepping stones to hit Sathankhamun.
*Other uber suggestions are [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]]/[[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Aku]] rushers/nukers, generalist tanks, generalist rushers and durable [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]].

