'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' This one isn't too difficult, but it sure does take a while. The moment the stage begins, spam Royal Guard Cats to take care of Nimoy Bore quickly, then use that cash to send out Cyberpunk Cat and Sniper the Deadeye. Ramen Cat can barely tank a hit from every threat here, making him the perfect stalling tool to facilitate Sniperpunk stacking. While sacrilegious, it is begrudgingly effective. The first pair are very likely to die, but you can get a second pair out on the field in due time.

Income is not abundant enough to afford the luxury of constantly spamming both Royal Guards and Ramen Cats, so if you start running low on cash, forego sending out Royal Guards for a while until you can recoup. You always want to be liquid enough to afford the next wave of Sniperpunks. Ideally, you should take out Chickful A and Mr. Puffington by the time the infinite Nimoy Bores start spawning, at which point, strive to get as many Sniperpunks out on the field. The more, the merrier. Go ahead and grab something to eat while your units go at it, as a matter of fact, I'll do just that.

